name: Unsupported dependency metadata clears stale claims and recovers after explicit correction
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_shapes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 20 LOGS | inventory-origin
submit: run sbom-scan:scan
require-live-snap: 30 sbom-scan: 3 components | first-inventory
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_shapes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART initial
submit: scene
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI VIZ | initial-gallery
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 20 COMPONENT STACK | initial-components
expect: owned-root
expect: compat-owned
expect: owned-child
keys: Escape
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 20 LOGS | invalid-input-origin
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_shapes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART break
submit: run sbom-scan:scan
require-live-snap: 30 devDependencies must be an object | invalid-input-result
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_shapes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART failed
submit: scene
require-live-snap: 20 Component inventory failed | failed-components
expect: packages/child/package.json
expect: devDependencies must be an object
expect-not: owned-root
expect-not: compat-owned
expect-not: owned-child
resize: 160x48
live-snap: failed-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: failed-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: failed-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: failed-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: failed-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: failure-page-1-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: failure-page-2-40x12
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_shapes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART failure-pages
ask: Does the failed nested manifest identify the unsupported field and provide keyboard-reachable recovery at every size without displaying the previous package claims?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 20 LOGS | correction-origin
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_shapes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART correct
submit: run sbom-scan:scan
require-live-snap: 30 sbom-scan: 3 components | corrected-inventory
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_shapes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART corrected
submit: scene
require-live-snap: 20 COMPONENT STACK | corrected-components
expect: owned-root
expect: compat-owned
expect: owned-child
expect: declared ^1.0
expect: declared ~2.0
expect: file:../shared
expect: Source freshness is unverified
expect-not: Map ✓
expect-not: Scan ✓
resize: 160x48
live-snap: corrected-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: corrected-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: corrected-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: corrected-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: corrected-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: corrected-page-1-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: corrected-page-2-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: corrected-page-3-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: corrected-page-4-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: corrected-page-5-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: corrected-page-6-40x12
ask: Is the corrected three-package inventory readable across the viewport matrix, with declared versions distinct from verified source or phase completion?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: scene
require-live-snap: 20 KUZUSHI VIZ | restart-gallery
keys: Tab
require-live-snap: 20 declared ^1.0 | restarted-components
expect: owned-root
expect: compat-owned
expect: owned-child
expect-not: Map ✓
expect-not: Scan ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/sbom_shapes.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart recollect the corrected inventory while retaining the failed and successful runs without new model calls, source execution or invented workflow progress?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
